{
  "family": "config-layers",
  "reference": "ts",
  "referenceVersion": "0.8.0",
  "sections": {
    "value_is_set": {
      "description": "Whether a value counts as set. `input.value` is the value; `input.missing: true` passes no value at all (Rust `None`, TypeScript `undefined`). `expect.set` is the answer.",
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "missing is not set",
          "input": {
            "missing": true
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "null is not set",
          "input": {
            "value": null
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "empty string is not set",
          "input": {
            "value": ""
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "whitespace-only string is not set",
          "input": {
            "value": "  \t"
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "text is set",
          "input": {
            "value": "x"
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "text with spaces around it is set",
          "input": {
            "value": " x "
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "the string 0 is set",
          "input": {
            "value": "0"
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "empty list is not set",
          "input": {
            "value": []
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "list with an item is set",
          "input": {
            "value": [
              1
            ]
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "list holding an empty string is set",
          "input": {
            "value": [
              ""
            ]
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "empty map is not set",
          "input": {
            "value": {}
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "map with a key is set",
          "input": {
            "value": {
              "a": null
            }
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "false is set",
          "input": {
            "value": false
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "true is set",
          "input": {
            "value": true
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "zero is set",
          "input": {
            "value": 0
          },
          "expect": {
            "set": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "value_at": {
      "description": "Look a dotted `key` up in `obj`. `expect.found` says whether the key is there, and `expect.value` is what it holds when it is.",
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "a top-level key",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "top"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": true,
            "value": "t"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a nested key",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.f.g"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": true,
            "value": "deep"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a nested mapping",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.f"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": true,
            "value": {
              "g": "deep"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "an empty string is found",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.b"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": true,
            "value": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "zero is found",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.c"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": true,
            "value": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "null is found",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.d"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": true,
            "value": null
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a list is found",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.e"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": true,
            "value": [
              1
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a missing top-level key",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "nope"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a missing nested key",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.nope"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "walking through a string",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "top.x"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "walking through null",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.d.x"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a key that contains a dot cannot be reached",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "dotted.key"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "an empty key",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": ""
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a list is not walked into",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.e.0"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "an inherited name is not a key",
          "input": {
            "obj": {
              "a": {
                "b": "",
                "c": 0,
                "d": null,
                "e": [
                  1
                ],
                "f": {
                  "g": "deep"
                }
              },
              "top": "t",
              "dotted.key": "x"
            },
            "key": "a.constructor"
          },
          "expect": {
            "found": false
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "yaml": {
      "description": "Read `input.yaml`, written to a file, as a config mapping (TypeScript `readMappingFile`, Rust `file::read_mapping`). `expect.mapping` is the mapping read. An error is `invalid_yaml` when the text does not parse or has a key that is not a scalar, and `not_a_mapping` when it parses to something other than a mapping.",
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "an empty file is an empty mapping",
          "input": {
            "yaml": ""
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "whitespace and comments only is an empty mapping",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "  \n# nothing set yet\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a bare null is an empty mapping",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "~\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "booleans, null, numbers and strings",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: true\nb: false\nc: null\nd: ~\ne: 1\nf: 1.5\ng: '1'\nh: text\ni: -3\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "a": true,
              "b": false,
              "c": null,
              "d": null,
              "e": 1,
              "f": 1.5,
              "g": "1",
              "h": "text",
              "i": -3
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "yes, no, on and off are strings",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: yes\nb: no\nc: on\nd: off\ne: Yes\nf: NO\ng: On\nh: OFF\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "a": "yes",
              "b": "no",
              "c": "on",
              "d": "off",
              "e": "Yes",
              "f": "NO",
              "g": "On",
              "h": "OFF"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "infinity and not-a-number read as their text",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: .inf\nb: -.inf\nc: .nan\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "a": ".inf",
              "b": "-.inf",
              "c": ".nan"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a scalar key is a string",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "1: a\ntrue: b\n2.5: c\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "1": "a",
              "true": "b",
              "2.5": "c"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "<< is an ordinary key",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "base: &b\n  x: 1\nderived:\n  <<: *b\n  y: 2\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "base": {
                "x": 1
              },
              "derived": {
                "<<": {
                  "x": 1
                },
                "y": 2
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "an alias to a scalar is that scalar",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: &x hello\nb: *x\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "a": "hello",
              "b": "hello"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a tag is dropped and the value kept",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: !!str 5\nb: !!int \"7\"\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "a": "5",
              "b": 7
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "nested mappings and sequences",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a:\n  b:\n    - 1\n    - two\n    - c: 3\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "a": {
                "b": [
                  1,
                  "two",
                  {
                    "c": 3
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a quoted number stays a string",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: '007'\nb: \"1e3\"\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "a": "007",
              "b": "1e3"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "octal and hex integers",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: 0o17\nb: 0x1F\n"
          },
          "expect": {
            "mapping": {
              "a": 15,
              "b": 31
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a duplicate key is an error",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: 1\na: 2\n"
          },
          "error": {
            "kind": "invalid_yaml"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a list key is an error",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "? [a]\n: x\n"
          },
          "error": {
            "kind": "invalid_yaml"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a mapping key is an error",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "? {a: 1}\n: x\n"
          },
          "error": {
            "kind": "invalid_yaml"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a null key is an error",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "~: x\n"
          },
          "error": {
            "kind": "invalid_yaml"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a list at the top level is an error",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "- a\n- b\n"
          },
          "error": {
            "kind": "not_a_mapping"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "a scalar at the top level is an error",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "just text\n"
          },
          "error": {
            "kind": "not_a_mapping"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "an unclosed flow sequence is an error",
          "input": {
            "yaml": "a: [1, 2\n"
          },
          "error": {
            "kind": "invalid_yaml"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "resolve_config_path": {
      "description": "Resolve a config value against `base_dir`, with `~` expanding to `home`. `expect.path` is the result. POSIX paths, so the cases run on Unix only.",
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "a bare word passes through",
          "input": {
            "value": "dev",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "dev"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a URL passes through",
          "input": {
            "value": "https://example.com/x",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "https://example.com/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a git URL passes through",
          "input": {
            "value": "ssh://git@host/x.git",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "ssh://git@host/x.git"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "an absolute path stays",
          "input": {
            "value": "/a/b",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/a/b"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a relative path joins the base",
          "input": {
            "value": "sub/x",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/sub/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a dot path joins the base",
          "input": {
            "value": "./x",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a dot-dot path walks up from the base",
          "input": {
            "value": "../x",
            "base_dir": "/base/proj",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "dot-dot inside a path is resolved",
          "input": {
            "value": "a/../b",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/b"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a dot file counts as a path",
          "input": {
            "value": ".config/x",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/.config/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "tilde alone is the home",
          "input": {
            "value": "~",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/home/me"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "tilde slash is under the home",
          "input": {
            "value": "~/x",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/home/me/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "tilde slash with a nested path",
          "input": {
            "value": "~/a/b",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/home/me/a/b"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "tilde user slash is not expanded",
          "input": {
            "value": "~user/x",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/~user/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "tilde user alone is not expanded",
          "input": {
            "value": "~user",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "/home/me"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/~user"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "an empty home leaves tilde slash unexpanded",
          "input": {
            "value": "~/x",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": ""
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/~/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "an empty home leaves tilde alone unexpanded",
          "input": {
            "value": "~",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": ""
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/~"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a relative home is used as given",
          "input": {
            "value": "~/x",
            "base_dir": "/base",
            "home": "rel"
          },
          "expect": {
            "path": "/base/rel/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "substitute_path_names": {
      "description": "Replace each `{name}` in `value` with its directory from `names`. `setting` names the setting in the error text, and `define_hint`, when given, takes the place of \"define it under paths:\" there. `expect.text` is the result. An unknown name is the error `unknown_path_name`, whose message every implementation gives word for word. POSIX paths, so the cases run on Unix only.",
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "no names in the value",
          "input": {
            "value": "/plain/path",
            "names": {
              "dev": "/home/me/dev",
              "work": "/work"
            },
            "setting": "repos:"
          },
          "expect": {
            "text": "/plain/path"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "one name",
          "input": {
            "value": "{dev}/checkouts",
            "names": {
              "dev": "/home/me/dev",
              "work": "/work"
            },
            "setting": "repos:"
          },
          "expect": {
            "text": "/home/me/dev/checkouts"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "two names",
          "input": {
            "value": "{dev}:{work}/x",
            "names": {
              "dev": "/home/me/dev",
              "work": "/work"
            },
            "setting": "repos:"
          },
          "expect": {
            "text": "/home/me/dev:/work/x"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "the same name twice",
          "input": {
            "value": "{dev}/{dev}",
            "names": {
              "dev": "/home/me/dev",
              "work": "/work"
            },
            "setting": "repos:"
          },
          "expect": {
            "text": "/home/me/dev//home/me/dev"
          },
          "platforms": [
            "unix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a name in the middle",
